  "final_answer": "The composite backlog is cleared against INT-09. All four deliverables are written to `/app` and confirmed.\n\nKey results:\n- **28 audited** requests (4 withdrawn \u2014 REQ-13/16/26/31 \u2014 excluded entirely), across **8 accounts**.\n- **14 flagged / 14 compliant**, **23 findings** total (character 6, background 5, consent 3, commercial 6, disclosure 3).\n- **4 accounts escalate**: ACC-02 and ACC-03 on the three-findings limb (REQ-05, REQ-10); ACC-07 and ACC-08 on share > 50% (ACC-08 also on three findings via REQ-30). The batch-wide flagged share is exactly 50%, so the \"strictly greater\" wording keeps ACC-01/04/05 at the intake desk despite tying it.\n- The memo flags the traps worth raising at review: the two **narrowing supersessions** (LIC-103\u2192LIC-109 cap 20 fails REQ-05; LIC-105\u2192LIC-110 scope `print_for_sale` fails REQ-28 but clears REQ-18), the **lapsed ACC-08 agreement** that is decisive for REQ-30's routing, and the **personal-use allowance** clearing character use that the cap would otherwise fail (notably REQ-32 at 55%).",
